00:36:33.965 --> 00:36:38.210
good plan in place to make that
that transition for sixty or

00:36:38.210 --> 00:36:41.330
seventy businesses
outside of the historic

00:36:41.330 --> 00:36:44.970
district to to make
that transition.

00:36:46.930 --> 00:36:49.370
I mentioned taking
care of what we have.

00:36:49.455 --> 00:36:52.015
One of the great tools that's
being implemented across the

00:36:52.015 --> 00:36:55.135
organization right now is
the Tyler Enterprise Resource

00:36:55.135 --> 00:36:57.695
Planning Program or ERP.

00:36:57.695 --> 00:37:01.055
And while we've done that
conversion on the finance side,

00:37:01.055 --> 00:37:04.170
we still have several
modules to move our

00:37:04.170 --> 00:37:09.690
systems and processes to,
including HR, payroll, etcetera.

00:37:09.690 --> 00:37:12.730
But honestly, one of the most powerful
things that we're gonna be converting

00:37:12.730 --> 00:37:16.570
to is the enterprise asset
management module through

00:37:16.570 --> 00:37:17.570
Tyler.

00:37:17.735 --> 00:37:21.415
What that means is that's going
to be able to centralize our

00:37:21.415 --> 00:37:24.455
our asset management and our

00:37:24.455 --> 00:37:29.015
workflow management into a into
a system that will allow us

00:37:29.015 --> 00:37:31.175
to better keep track of
all the assets we have.

00:37:31.175 --> 00:37:33.710
And when you think about what
the all the assets the town

00:37:33.710 --> 00:37:34.990
has, this is, you know,

00:37:34.990 --> 00:37:39.070
this is anything from a street
sign all the way to water and

00:37:39.070 --> 00:37:41.710
sewer lines and
everything in between.

00:37:41.710 --> 00:37:45.630
And it'll be based
in a in a GIS so

00:37:45.630 --> 00:37:49.015
that we can track
those things not

00:37:49.015 --> 00:37:52.535
just on paper, but
visually on a map as well.

00:37:52.535 --> 00:37:55.175
And so this is gonna be a big
this is gonna be a big cultural

00:37:55.175 --> 00:37:58.935
shift for the organization in
terms of more effectively and

00:37:58.935 --> 00:38:01.950
efficiently being able to
manage our assets and keep

00:38:01.950 --> 00:38:04.710
track of things, be
able to replace them.

00:38:04.750 --> 00:38:08.030
You know, I'd another
example would be,

00:38:08.030 --> 00:38:11.310
if we fill a pothole on
a street in the town,

00:38:11.310 --> 00:38:14.670
how many more times do we go back
to that same pothole to refill it?

00:38:14.670 --> 00:38:17.455
That's the type of data that
we'll be able to have and track

00:38:17.455 --> 00:38:20.335
and understand the assets
that we're dealing with.

00:38:20.335 --> 00:38:24.335
So very, very powerful game
changer for team Warrenton and

00:38:24.335 --> 00:38:29.055
our our ability to operate
and manage our assets

00:38:29.055 --> 00:38:30.975
and and all the
workflows as well.

00:38:30.975 --> 00:38:32.495
So I'm excited to
see that through.

00:38:32.495 --> 00:38:36.110
It's, again, gonna be a pretty
big shift for the organization.

00:38:36.150 --> 00:38:37.190
And finally,

00:38:37.190 --> 00:38:39.750
the the best part of that
program is that there's going

00:38:39.750 --> 00:38:42.710
